From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:43:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: set the output phase for DDR on new-timing hosts

Writing in DDR52 on the H616 eMMC controller leaves a request uncompleted
after a while: a data error, or none, then the status command in recovery
never returns. Allwinner's own driver drives the command line at 180
degrees and, in DDR, the data lines at 180 too; this driver never touched
the drive delay register. Set it as the vendor driver does.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index 8dbcff5..b411a4d 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -222,6 +222,10 @@
 
 #define SDXC_2X_TIMING_MODE	BIT(31)
 
+/* Drive delay control */
+#define SDXC_CMD_DRV_PH_180	BIT(16)
+#define SDXC_DAT_DRV_PH_180	BIT(17)
+
 #define SDXC_CAL_START		BIT(15)
 #define SDXC_CAL_DONE		BIT(14)
 #define SDXC_CAL_DL_SHIFT	8
@@ -839,6 +843,20 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_clk_set_rate(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host,
 		mmc_writel(host, REG_SD_NTSR, rval);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The output phase of Allwinner's own driver: command at 180 degrees,
+	 * data at 180 in DDR and 90 otherwise.
+	 */
+	if (host->use_new_timings) {
+		rval = mmc_readl(host, REG_DRV_DL) | SDXC_CMD_DRV_PH_180;
+		if (ios->timing == MMC_TIMING_MMC_DDR52 ||
+		    ios->timing == MMC_TIMING_UHS_DDR50)
+			rval |= SDXC_DAT_DRV_PH_180;
+		else
+			rval &= ~SDXC_DAT_DRV_PH_180;
+		mmc_writel(host, REG_DRV_DL, rval);
+	}
+
 	/* sunxi_mmc_clk_set_phase expects the actual card clock rate */
 	ret = sunxi_mmc_clk_set_phase(host, ios, rate);
 	if (ret)
